<section class="inner-sec">
  <div class="sec-eyebrow">How it works in a firm</div>
  <h2>Every caller handled, every good lead qualified</h2>
  <p class="lede">One receptionist covers the phone, the texts, and the website — answering what's routine, screening what's new, and leaving the actual accounting to you.</p>
  <div class="svc-grid">
    <div class="svc"><strong>Missed-call text-back</strong>A call you can't take becomes a text conversation instead of a voicemail you'll return at nine tonight.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Answers the usuals</strong>Hours, location, what you charge to prepare, what to bring, deadlines and extension dates — answered instantly, any hour.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Screens new clients</strong>Individual or business, entity type, which services, roughly what scale — captured before the call reaches you, so you know if it's a fit.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Books consults</strong>Qualified prospects go straight onto your calendar for an intro call — not into a queue you work through on Sunday.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Chases documents</strong>Automatic follow-ups to the clients still sitting on their W-2s, 1099s, or signed engagement letter.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Human handoff</strong>Anything that touches actual advice, a notice, or an existing return goes to you with a summary of the conversation.</div>
  </div>
</section>

