<section class="inner-sec" style="padding-top: 10px;">
  <div class="proof-band">
    <div class="sec-eyebrow">Confidentiality by design</div>
    <h2>Built to never discuss a client's return</h2>
    <p>Your front desk answers logistics — hours, pricing, what to bring, deadlines, how to get started — and routes everything else to you. It doesn't ask for, store, or discuss Social Security numbers, income figures, filings, or IRS correspondence. That's deliberate: a front desk should get people to you, not handle what only you should handle.</p>
    <div class="proof-points">
      <div class="ppoint">
        <strong>Front-desk facts only</strong>
        <span>It answers operational questions and books consults. Anything about a specific return, notice, or number goes straight to your team.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ppoint">
        <strong>No sensitive data collected</strong>
        <span>It captures a name, a number, and a reason to follow up — never an SSN, EIN, account balance, or document contents.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ppoint">
        <strong>Screening you actually control</strong>
        <span>You set the qualifying questions, so the leads that reach your calendar match the work you want and the clients you'd take.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ppoint">
        <strong>Busiest season, same coverage</strong>
        <span>It doesn't get overwhelmed in March. The hundredth caller of the day gets the same answer as the first, at the same speed.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

